    {
     "e": "🥪✖️",
     "t": "Multiplying is adding equal groups. A sandwich costs LE 4, so 6 sandwiches cost 6 × 4 = LE 24."
    },
    {
     "e": "🔄",
     "t": "We can multiply in any order: 7 × 5 = 5 × 7 = 35. This is called the commutative law."
    },
    {
     "e": "🔟",
     "t": "To multiply by 10, the digits move one place left: 10 × 7 = 70 and 80 × 4 = 320 (8 × 4 = 32, then ×10)."
    },
    {
     "e": "➗🍪",
     "t": "Dividing is sharing into equal groups. 35 ÷ 5 = 7 and 48 ÷ 4 = 12. Dividing by 10 moves digits right: 490 ÷ 10 = 49."
    },
    {
     "e": "🧩",
     "t": "Sometimes there is a remainder. 63 ÷ 5 = 12 remainder 3, because 12 × 5 = 60 and 3 are left over."
    },
    {
     "e": "⭐🔵",
     "t": "Iman needs 55 circles. Each sticker sheet has 5 circles. 55 ÷ 5 = 11 sheets."
    },
    {
     "e": "🧠",
     "t": "Know your tables! Numbers in the 5 times table end in 0 or 5. Numbers in the 4 times table are all even: 8, 36 ..."
    }
   ]
